Z||000003||Tina||12-20-2000||11:14 PM||||Wouldn't mind be seen in one of them but 190 horsies.Babe-magnet? Perhaps!!<BR>Your right about the compressing part,no detailed info to be found on engine. And all the germans are still tucked away in bed.<BR>7+ time difference.So no answers yet from the other side of pond.<P>Engine 2,295-cc intercooled supercharged DOHC<BR>16-valve inline-4, alloy cylinder head.<P>Net Power 190 hp @ 5,500 rpm<P>Net torque 200 lb-ft @ 2,500-4,800 rpm<P>Compression ratio 9.0:1<P>Fuel Requirement Premium unleaded, 91 pump octane.<P>Fuel and ignition systems ME 2.1 fully electronic<BR>sequential multipoint fuel injection and ignition with<BR>individual cylinder control of fuel spray and spark<BR>timing. Electronic throttle.<P>Intake system Variable intake-valve timing. Belt-driven<BR>supercharger with liquid-to-air intercooler to further<BR>increase intake air density.<P>Manual Transmission Standard fully synchronized<BR>6-speed manual with clutch-starter interlock. <P>Baseprice in U.S $38.900.00 for econo<BR>0 to 100kph  7.9sec<BR>topspeed  231 kph<P>Too tired to find calulator but in every mile are 1.6 Kilometer  <p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
