Z||000007||WampusCat||12-20-2000||11:39 PM||||That price was for the normally aspirated model.  Expect to pay around $50k for the supercharged "Kompressor."  I've never driven one but the reviews from Car and Driver basically said it was a fine convertable touring car for cruising the antique markets but it's not a sports car.  They were pretty harsh in their descriptions of it's handling on the track.  It came in way last in a comparison with the Boxster, BMW M roadster and the Honda S2000.  I've seen a few around here, all driven by women so maybe it is a "chick magnet."||||reg||1
