Z||000011||WampusCat||12-21-2000||10:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>WampusCat, are you sure about that.<BR>Baseprice on the their website is 38.9 for the SLK 230  <BR>Tina</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Oops, You're right.  All the 230's are supercharged.  [note to self: check facts before posting and looking like a dolt.] The 2001 prices were reduced $2100 from last year's base price of $41000 according to Edmund's.  There are several articles on Car and Driver's website including a long term test.  Just use the search function for "slk."  <A HREF="http://www.caranddriver.com" TARGET=_blank>www.caranddriver.com</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Seanh||12-21-2000||11:17 PM||||Honestly, I am not a fan of the "lower priced" encono merc's. I have driven two. One was a 96 320 SLK, nice, very smooth riding, and very quiet. Unfortunatly, we were only adding 2 subs, so we didnt get to keep it very long. I have also driven a 93 560 Convertable. Wow, now that thing hauled like nothin before. I was so suprised. Nailed a speed bump at about 45 mph and couldnt even feel it (This was a personal friend of mine, don't want you to think I take other peoples cars out and beat them when I am working on stereo's) I hate the stereo systems in them. Such a pain in the a$$. All fiber optic system, running from headunit to amp, and speaker wire to the speakers. Those things are such a hassel since only a few companies make F/O headunits. So if you get one, make sure you get the Premiem sound system because you dont want to pay to have it upgraded later.||||reg||1
Z||000013||baldlobo||12-21-2000||11:24 PM||||Don't get me started; my parents have 1972 350SL(the L is suppost to stand for light, only if you count 3500lbs light <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||12-23-2000||08:33 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baldlobo:<BR><B>Don't get me started; my parents have 1972 350SL(the L is suppost to stand for light, only if you count 3500lbs light   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i have the same body type, only its an AMG 560SL, its fun and fast, still like my Ferrari/Fiero better though. Their as fast as a vette, ride like a caddy with the weight. they were lite for their day, remember caddys and lincolns used to weight 5000-6000 pnds<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cheever2||12-23-2000||11:33 PM||||Well, since this is still an active topic, I saw one today I liked better but wasn't as small.  It was a 500, had a S-something, maybe it was SL500, don't remember.  But it sure was a good looking car.<P>I see lots of sports cars around Houston.  Ferrari's are everywhere here.  See NSX's all the time, they're one of the few cars lower than mine.  Rode next to a new red Lotus the other day for a few blocks.  VERY nice.  I would gladly kick the Fiero habit for one of those.  Recently saw a red Diablo.  Occassionally see some good old classic musclecars, but no more than in  other cities.  Come Spring I'll be getting motorcycle fever again, but never gave in to it.  My older brother in Tulsa is a Harley guy but I don't understand what the attraction is, I never wanted one of those.  He has a webpage... <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5050/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5050/index.html</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 12-23-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000016||rogergarrison||12-24-2000||07:28 AM||||Ill tell ya cheever, ive got friends that have the real deal exotics. TestaRosa, Pantera, Lotus, Jags. One friend even traded a second house for a Lambo. Every one of them has lots of expensive problems. The lambo broke down everysingle time he drove it, just one little small thing after another. It would melt the 345 tires off if he held the gas, but one day itd be radiator, next, alternator, next door lock-after a year he couldnt wait to get rid of it. This was one reason I chose to build a replica, has all the style, goes just as good, very little maintainence. My whole engine blueprinted with a turbo hasnt cost me $5,000. My friends TestaRosa cost him $3800 just for a clutch and a rebuilt long block is over $25,000.||||reg||1
